{"c":[{"id":"41a7747c68ff4b5e","sum":"U1: panel windows +24 pt for shadow except the desk; ContrastRenderTests gate contrast from pixels; off-screen NSHostingView has no a11y tree; mkdir ModelRuntime/Vendor before llama.xcframework. Never-typed kinds: memory/sensitive.ts only. T2 range edits are AX-only, never paste.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"b12c5adbb4da292e","sum":"U1: panel frames are the content's; windows +24 pt for shadow except the desk (margin 0). ContrastRenderTests gate 4.5 text / 3 marks from pixels. Off-screen NSHostingView has no a11y tree: test via SlipSpeech. Setup: mkdir ModelRuntime/Vendor before copying llama.xcframework.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"caa08afcda9d84a4","sum":"U1: HostedPanel frames are the content's; windows are 24 pt larger for the drawn shadow, except interactive panels (desk: margin 0, system shadow). ContrastRenderTests measure token contrast from rendered pixels; a slip under 4.5 text / 3 marks fails there.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T205314Z-27bd8497da5b0b8f","text":"U1 v3: HostedPanel frames (size, pin, debugInfo) are the content's; the window is 24 pt larger for the drawn shadow, except interactive panels (the desk), which keep margin 0 and the system shadow so the margin never eats clicks.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T205315Z-15530fcef19ed7a7","text":"U1: token contrast is measured from rendered pixels by ContrastRenderTests (Tokens.hidden blanks one token; changed pixels are its glyphs, the hidden render is their ground); a token change that drops a slip under 4.5 text / 3 marks fails there.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"1e56ade2067e19a9","sum":"Worktree setup: mkdir packages/keytype/Packages/ModelRuntime/Vendor before copying llama.xcframework, or Vendor becomes the framework. Off-screen NSHostingView has no a11y tree; test slip labels via SlipSpeech, count elements only on screen (VM).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T205315Z-c430e28338d1fa45","text":"Worktree setup: copying llama.xcframework into packages/keytype/Packages/ModelRuntime/Vendor/ when Vendor does not exist makes Vendor the framework (SwiftPM: 'does not contain a binary artifact'); mkdir Vendor first.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T205315Z-d04a530977d6b116","text":"U1: SwiftUI builds no accessibility tree for an NSHostingView that is not on screen (accessibilityChildren is empty even after cacheDisplay); test slip labels through SlipSpeech, count elements only on screen (VM).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"d3c90c2874f43484","sum":"B25: spaced eval calls need a fresh AbortSignal; realfill strips U+2731 from labels. Never-typed kinds: extend memory/sensitive.ts only. T2: writing marks bind to their checked sentence (an edit there drops one); range edits are AX-only (select, revalidate, verify), never paste.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"b1d476e32a92cb95","sum":"B25: eval writers that space calls need a fresh AbortSignal after the wait (a 15 s gap aborted every intent). The job form marks required labels with U+2731; realfill normLabel strips it (B24 scoreboards missed those four fields).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T211051Z-3925313f151b5275","text":"B25: eval writers that space calls must give the request a fresh AbortSignal after the wait; a 15 s gap aborted every intent in planner-eval's first GUI run.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T211051Z-9174d67891bff255","text":"B25: the job form marks required labels with U+2731; realfill normLabel strips it, and B24's scoreboards counted those four fields as not found.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"a514cda7aa8cec1f","sum":"Never-typed kinds live in memory/sensitive.ts (M1); extend it, no second list. T2: writing fixes are OfferKind.writing; a mark binds to its checked sentence, any edit there drops it; range edits are AX-only (select, revalidate, AXSelectedText, verify), never paste.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T211051Z-bc8230171f42cb4e","text":"B25: never-typed kinds (fill, planner, Ask) are memory/sensitive.ts, M1's classifier copied unchanged from v2/memory; extend that file, never a second list.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T212904Z-afa8d900ec44c553","text":"T2: writing fixes are OfferKind.writing; a mark is bound to its checked sentence (WritingMarks), so any edit in that sentence (or its '. ' before) drops it; range edits are AX-only (select, revalidate, AXSelectedText, caret back, verify), never paste.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"cfcfde6b45075d98","sum":"Spelling uses US/GB/CA witnesses; build-app.sh holds build.lock (CARET_NO_LOCK=1 under lockf); SIP off here; Caret.app starts own services unless a socket is named, tests use --home; acting debug commands need --test-hooks; captcha HSTS; SO_NOSIGPIPE; Groq TPD 429s.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"b3ea4773732e5218","sum":"T2: NativeChecker uses US/GB/CA witnesses (en_AU accepts 'seperate'); NSSpellChecker may autocorrect to guess 2. H4: build-app.sh holds build.lock (CARET_NO_LOCK=1 under lockf); SIP is off here; Caret.app starts its own services unless a socket is named; tests pass --home.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"cc86c50101fc2328","sum":"T2: en_AU accepts 'seperate'/'truely', so NativeChecker uses US/GB/CA witnesses; NSSpellChecker may autocorrect to its 2nd guess (adress->dress). H4: build-app.sh holds build.lock all run; callers under heavy.sh/lockf set CARET_NO_LOCK=1; release/acceptance need IDENTITY.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T212904Z-f841172a94ee81e8","text":"T2: macOS 26.6's en_AU spell dictionary accepts 'seperate' and 'truely'; NativeChecker uses US/GB/CA as regional witnesses and en-AU only when the user lists it. In context NSSpellChecker can autocorrect to its 2nd guess ('adress' -> dress while guess 1 is address).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T220029Z-2e8d5e2431d5ac81","text":"H4: build-app.sh takes build.lock for the whole run (compile, copy, sign); a caller already under heavy.sh or lockf sets CARET_NO_LOCK=1 or it deadlocks. release and acceptance need IDENTITY (team cert SHA-1); debug is ad hoc.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"0b2cc0daa10616a1","sum":"H4: SIP is off on Sam's Mac, so hardened runtime/library validation aren't enforced; measure entitlements on a SIP-on Mac. A built Caret.app starts its own helper and reader unless --helper-socket or CARET_SCREEN_SOCKET names one; test runs pass --home DIR.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T220029Z-8a608f67782b76c4","text":"H4: SIP is disabled on Sam's Mac (csrutil status), so the hardened runtime and library validation are not enforced there; node.entitlements (allow-jit only) and any entitlement question must be measured on a SIP-on Mac.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T220029Z-91a1d68b9a61d85a","text":"H4: a built Caret.app starts its own helper and reader unless --helper-socket or CARET_SCREEN_SOCKET names one; test runs of a bundle pass --home DIR (sockets, data, host.sock and settings move there) and never run with neither.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"030d4823d12628cf","sum":"Debug socket key/control/click/settings set need --test-hooks. Captcha hosts are HSTS: test frames via compose.ts unit tests. Bridge Swift tests share a process: test sockets need SO_NOSIGPIPE. Groq one-token probes pass with TPD spent; only real-size requests show 429.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"90700581377d9b92","sum":"CodeRabbit #9: the debug socket refuses key, control, click and settings set without --test-hooks; key-driving scripts pass it. W4: captcha hosts are HSTS-preloaded, so a test browser can't map them to local http; test captcha frames via extension compose.ts unit tests.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T220029Z-fe7551bbc4c0644b","text":"CodeRabbit #9: the host debug socket refuses key, control, click and settings set without --test-hooks (HostRuntime.testHookRefusal); acceptance scripts that drive keys start the host with --test-hooks.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T220624Z-f865060dd10d04a3","text":"W4: hcaptcha/recaptcha hosts are HSTS-preloaded, so --host-resolver-rules cannot point a test browser's captcha frame at a local http server (the load hangs); test captcha frame composition through extension/src/worker/compose.ts unit tests instead.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"1c32ace5fe4e098f","sum":"W4: Swift Testing runs bridge tests in one process; a fixture-accepted test socket needs SO_NOSIGPIPE or a late write kills the run (signal 13). B26: Groq answers a one-token probe even with a model's tokens-per-day spent; only a real-size request shows the 429.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T223033Z-e64c70b59e406a7f","text":"W4: Swift Testing runs bridge tests in one process; a test socket that a fixture accept()s needs SO_NOSIGPIPE, or a write after the peer closed kills the whole run with signal 13, blamed on whichever test was running.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T224111Z-04a43869ad872043","text":"B26: Groq answers a one-token probe even when a model's tokens-per-day is spent; only a real-size request shows the 429 TPD. gpt-oss-120b's day ran out during B26's first Ask run.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
